# JavaScript

Keep **vanilla** ES6+. No React, no bundler, no new frameworks.

## File boundaries

| File | Owns |
|------|------|
| `js/common.js` | Mobile menu, smooth scroll, shared animations, floating contact UI on multi pages |
| `js/contact.js` | Contact page validation, FAQ toggles, FormSubmit success UX |
| `js/insights.js` | Insights listing search/filter + newsletter `#newsletter-thanks` hash UX |

Put shared behavior in `common.js`. Keep contact-only logic in `contact.js`. Keep insights listing behavior in `insights.js`. Avoid duplicating listeners across files.

## Do not break

- Mobile menu open/close and overlay
- Smooth scroll / in-page anchors (services)
- FAQ accordion toggles on contact
- Form validation feedback users already rely on

## Forms note

- Contact page: real FormSubmit POST (see `pages/contact.html`).
- Homepage floating `#quick-contact-form`: posts via FormSubmit (same pattern as contact). Do not silently change fields / `_next` / email without an explicit product request.

## Scripts

Pages load scripts via relative `<script src="…">`. After moves, confirm paths for root vs `pages/`.
